  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: a standard linear dimensionality reduction (PCA to 2000 dims) on a single RNA profile with no learned encoder, aggregation, or fusion. This isolates the raw signal in the RNA data without confounding from complex encoders or multimodal fusion. It answers the foundational question: 'How much accuracy is achievable from basic RNA features alone?' This floor is essential before interpreting whether learned encoders (scVI, scGPT), multiprofile aggregation, image modalities, or multimodal fusion add meaningful value. Choosing the simplest model first also minimizes the risk of training instability or hyperparameter sensitivity confounding the first data point. With 9 experiments remaining, this baseline enables a structured build-up: compare to image-only (config_010), then to better RNA encoders (config_004/007), then to multimodal (config_016), each step isolating one design dimension."
}

